vmsa:
=====
2 levels of page tables:
12 + 8 + 12 (actual page)

middle one is the page table and is of 1k size with 256 entries. Each entry either points to 4K or 64K page.

When pointing to 64K page, all 16 entries have the same value.


1MB pages are formed by the PDE directly pointing to the page
16 PDEs pointing to the same 16MB page is called a Super Section.

TTBR0 and TTBR1 store address of the page directory. There are two based on what the top `n' bits 
of the MVA are. TTBCR controls the value of `n'.
This allows kernel and user spaces to share different page tables and not cause reprogramming on 
context switch.


Global/nGlobal bits in the PTE tell the TLB to not discard Global entries on context switch (CONTEXTIDR) changes.
